Description: GT IPTV Player Pro for Enigma2
 Xtream Codes, M3U and Stalker/MAC accounts with Live TV, Movies and Series.
 Selectable user-data backup and restore with section sizes and safety copies.
 Multi-day EPG guide, previous-channel recall and redesigned information bar.
 All Movies browsing and account-wide movie search for Xtream and Stalker.
 Persistent, progressive movie search with resumable category checkpoints.
 Paged normal movie browsing through the same streaming catalogue on Xtream.
 Streamed All Series and category browsing with an independent series cache.
 Persistent watched-episode ticks across playback, resume, seeking and receiver restarts.
 Immediate BLUE-key account-wide series search with season/episode selection.
 Optional 14-poster movie/series grid with details and vertical page navigation.
 Writable cache selection and a portable backend for images without SQLite.
 Optional single-account automatic login with a translated connection overlay.
 Shared weather and receiver incoming network rate in Mbps.
 Actual video resolution in information bars and YouTube previews.
 YouTube infobar thumbnails, a local logo fallback and correct source details.
 Live guide with the upcoming schedule on the left and a large poster below mini-TV.
 Current-programme posters use TMDb, TVmaze and a bounded 10 MiB temporary cache.
 Permanent removal from Downloads with a separate choice to keep or delete files.
 Bounded background jobs, fair artwork caching and batched native image updates.
 Prepared page backgrounds with bounded, cancellation-safe screen handoffs.
 Visible-only CPU/RAM dial percentages and a one-second information-bar clock.
 Nonblocking account/download/favorite actions and ordered asynchronous resume saves.
 Bounded movie/series windows, batched catalogue queries and cancellable image transfers.
 Provider metadata language preference and original YouTube audio selection.
 User interface translated into 43 device languages.
 TMDb-verified subtitle identities, strict episode checks and conservative release matching.
 Seven portrait cinema cards and bounded visible-poster download/decode recovery.
 Independent subtitle timing keys 4/5/6, minute-range offsets and non-modal feedback.
 Configurable infobar auto-hide: Off or 1-10 seconds, default 4, localized in 43 languages.
 Bounded artwork and XMLTV caches, shared glass surfaces and background subtitle restore.
 Remove baked empty poster frames from movie and series backgrounds; existing glass theme retained.
 Prepare adjacent VOD posters and cinematic artwork with bounded native caching and immediate cached details.
 Prioritize selected and adjacent cinematic heroes independently of full metadata while preserving bounded page preparation.
 Keep the displayed cinematic hero visible until replacement artwork is decoded; preserve selection cancellation and bounded preparation.
 Remove the MENU hold shortcut caption and badge from playback information bars.
 Cinematic season and episode browser with shaded series artwork and native remote navigation.
 Durable completion dates, season progress and direct resume with watched/unwatched control.
 Refined series title size and transparent borderless episode remote guide.
 Native-size episode action frames retain complete borders across receiver resolutions.
 Localized subtitle timing feedback, plural-aware counters and refreshed language headings.
 Browser-language server diagnostics, validation reasons, delete confirmations and M3U labels.
 Preserve pending resumes and restored history; report durable-save failures accurately.
 Nonblocking portal refresh, retryable catalog pages and verified complete M3U bodies.
 Transactional download state, safe concurrent metadata/artwork and YouTube start/end checks.
 Bounded standalone web requests and paged episode selection.
 Local SRT/VTT subtitle browser with HDD/USB/NAS storage and readable download filenames.
 Local subtitle synchronization and resume; translated local-file controls in all 43 languages.
 Immediate cached live-programme posters with bounded latest-selection workers and cancellable transfers.
 Combined movie/TV poster lookup, limited selected-channel EPG recovery and per-stage timing diagnostics.
 Full receiver-folder navigation for local subtitle search and download destinations, including linked directories.
 Scoped VOD category timeout and timing diagnostics; explicit Xtream category browsing identity.
 Restore settings backups by supported archive format independently of plugin release numbers.
